    "billPage": 0,
    "chapter": 0,
    "lineEnd": 0,
    "lineStart": 0,
    "memoText": "\n                         VETO MESSAGE - No. 542\n\nTO THE ASSEMBLY:\n\nI am returning herewith, without my approval, the following bill:\n\nAssembly Bill Number 8583, entitled:\n\n    \"AN  ACT  to  amend  the public service law, in relation to hearings\n      following major power outages\"\n\n    NOT APPROVED\n\n  This bill would require that  after  every  major  power  outage,  the\nPublic  Service  Commission (PSC) schedule at least one public statement\nhearing in each affected county, city with a population  of  150,000  or\nmore,  or  New  York  City borough if such a hearing is requested by the\nrelevant locality. The PSC would also be  required  to  publish  on  its\nwebsit  a  report  summarizing  the  hearing  and any recommended policy\nchanges the hearing may have initiated, and to send the report to  vari-\nous state and local officials.\n\n  The  goal of this bill is laudable. However, the bill fails to account\nfor existing PSC processes  regarding  post-outage  investigations  that\ninclude public hearings as well as staff field investigations and inter-\nviews,  evaluations  of complaint data, analysis of information required\nto be filed  by  utilities,  and  reviews  of  emergency  response  plan\nperformance  and  utility  communications with the public and government\nofficials. In addition, investigations are published  on  PSC's  website\nand  shared with all utilities. This bill, by requiring multiple, dupli-\ncative hearings, would  result  in  inefficient  procedures  that  could\ndistract  from  the goal of restoring service after an outage. For these\nreasons, I am vetoing this bill. I am, however, directing the Department\nof Public Service to conduct at least one  public  hearing  following  a\nmajor  outage  in a location convenient to customers within the affected\ngeographic area.\n\n  The bill is disapproved.                    (signed) ANDREW M. CUOMO\n\n                               __________\n",
    "signedDate": null,
    "signer": "ANDREW M. CUOMO",
    "vetoNumber": 542,
    "vetoType": "STANDARD",
    "year": 2014
   }
